// TERMINATION-RANKING-CHECKS asks to "recover executable customers from
// `rank_remainder_endpoints` and `rank_endpoint_borrows` (deleted in
// `c60792d7bdd`) as ordinary corpus entries", the second being "a countdown
// whose bound is reached through a stored exclusive reference". This is that
// program, recovered from `c60792d7bdd^` and wrapped so it asserts its own
// result. It does NOT check yet, which is why it is pinned here rather than
// landed in `pass/`.
//
// Its SIBLING does check. The remainder-endpoints countdown -- a named-state
// walk whose operands are REORDERED across the transition
// (`walk(remaining, cap, divisor)` -> `iterate(divisor, cap, remaining)`)
// while `cap % divisor` endpoints are preserved -- checks clean today and is
// ready for `pass/termination/` as soon as `tests/omega/corpus_outcomes.txt`
// is free to record its row. It was held by another lane when this landed.
//
// What blocks THIS one is not ranking. Three one-change controls:
//
//   let mut owner: Wrap = Wrap { remaining: 6 };          checks
//   ... then `let r: &mut Wrap = &mut owner;`             OMITTED at
//                          `statement sequence: unsupported statement kind`
//   ... then `Indirect { target: &mut owner }`            OMITTED at
//                 `statement sequence: local data: structural call binding`
//
// So the record literal is fine and the ranking contract is fine; a `&mut`
// borrow of a plain LOCAL has no route, and carrying one in a record literal
// field has none either. Both are REFERENCE-LOCAL-BINDING-ROUTES, whose
// fixture records that a reference binding routes only for a `&mut` of a
// SELF-rooted place named directly. A record literal with a REFERENCE field
// is one more producer for that item's list.
//
// Acceptance when that clears: this checks, interprets, and returns native 0.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Wrap { remaining: u64 [4..=500]; }
data Indirect { target: &mut Wrap; }

machine walk(n: u64 [0..=4], indirect: Indirect)
terminates by n -> Nat::Descending in 0..=indirect.target.remaining;
-> u64 {
    transition n > 0 {
        true -> walk(n - 1, indirect)
        false -> n
    }
}

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    let mut owner: Wrap = Wrap { remaining: 6 };
    let indirect: Indirect = Indirect { target: &mut owner };
    let settled: u64 = walk(4, indirect);

    transition settled == 0 {
        true -> good(&mut self)
        _ -> bad(&mut self)
    }

    state good(main: &mut Main) { main.console.exit_process(0); }
    state bad(main: &mut Main) { main.console.exit_process(1); }
}
